rt-bdj.jar holds classes and files of the OpenJDK 8 runtime (GPLv2 with the Classpath Exception; see LICENSE and
ASSEMBLY_EXCEPTION), unmodified, selected by src/bdj-classlib/classes.txt and tools/bdj-classlib/resources.txt.
The one exception is lib/security/cacerts, the keystore ca-certificates-java 20240118
generates from ca-certificates 20260601~24.04.1: its entries' creation dates are set to
2026-10-15T00:00:00Z (tools/bdj-classlib/normalize-jks.py) so the jar is reproducible.

Third-party code among those classes:
- com/sun/org/apache/xerces/internal/** (Apache Xerces Java, as bundled in OpenJDK's JAXP) and
  com/sun/xml/internal/stream/Entity*: Apache License 2.0. The JDK's notice for its Apache components, with the
  license text, is THIRD_PARTY_APACHE (from the JDK's THIRD_PARTY_README; it carries no separate Xerces NOTICE
  file). The other JAXP classes (javax/xml/parsers, jdk/xml/internal, the rest of com/sun/xml/internal/stream) are
  GPLv2 with the Classpath Exception.
- org/xml/sax/**: SAX, GPLv2 with the Classpath Exception in OpenJDK plus the SAX project's public-domain
  notice (SAX_NOTICE).

